# Citation metadata for release v0.1.0. No DOI has been assigned; none is listed. The release
# commit is recorded in the release build manifest, not in this file.
# No license field: there is no repository-wide license. Licensing is scoped per file (LICENSE):
# MIT only for seven original harness files, CC BY-NC 4.0 for five files adapted from
# SamsungLabs/LittleBit, all rights reserved for everything else (documentation, results, data).
# A single SPDX value here would misstate that.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you refer to this audit, please cite it as below, and cite the LittleBit papers for the
  methods. This is a deployment audit of existing research code, not a new method.
type: software
title: >-
  LittleBit deployment audit: packed sign serialization, storage accounting and a tiny
  real-model wiring pilot
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-08"
authors:
  - family-names: Urista
    given-names: Tim
repository-code: "https://github.com/timurista/littlebit-deployment-audit"
url: "https://github.com/timurista/littlebit-deployment-audit/releases/tag/v0.1.0"
abstract: >-
  An audit of the packed serialization path and storage accounting of SamsungLabs/LittleBit at
  commit 933857ed1443b53fc43a875c2cf64249e3c56f0c. The shipped unpacker decodes a -1 sign only at
  in-word position 0: in an exhaustive sweep of 2,010 sign patterns through the upstream functions,
  296 decode exactly and 21,881 signs flip from -1 to +1; the packer is correct and a one-line
  change restores all 2,010 cases. Storage accounting separates advertised bits per weight,
  serialized file bytes and resident float bytes. A tiny bounded CPU wiring pilot on
  Qwen2.5-0.5B (16 QAT steps, 2,048 training tokens, 1,016 scored held-out tokens, one seed) is
  included as a harness check; it is not a benchmark and not a replication of any published
  LittleBit result.
keywords:
  - quantization
  - binary factorization
  - serialization
  - reproducibility
  - audit
